The Necessity of the Last Judgment

A court is only necessary in any system, large or small, when something has gone seriously wrong and the wisest possible decision must be made to stabilize that system or a social order.

In many easy, favorable cases, it is only a matter of mediation: When we humans meet in our earthly courts, it is often because personal interests of some kind collide with one another and the differences of opinion are so entrenched that a decision must be made by a stranger, the judge, which ideally relates and balances the interests of the opponents as fairly as possible.

The whole thing becomes much more serious when a person appears in court because he has violated social rules that are indispensable for reasonable coexistence, be it for example fraud or theft, negligent recklessness that has harmed fellow human beings and much more, up to and including efforts to override social rules in a way that endangers the state. In this case, the judge must ideally try to bring about compensation for the injured party and impose a tangible consequence for the perpetrator so that he can hopefully avoid such actions in the future.

If it is a matter of more or less serious crimes that harm other people and society, the perpetrator must be separated from other people for a longer or shorter period of time, depending on the severity of the crime and his or her ability to understand, until he or she has either recognized and regretted his or her crime so that he or she can be reintegrated into society , or, if the risk is too high, must be permanently separated to protect others .

All of this is also necessary for a fair justice system. Even if many courts, systems and entire states pass unjust, arbitrary or even criminal judgments against humanity, this can only be blamed on human abuse of the laws of justice, but fundamentally does not change the basis of what has been said. -

"As in small things, so in large things!" The great world judgment, which is increasingly affecting the human race on earth, follows the same basic rules. In this case too, something has gone seriously wrong, because humanity has clearly and unmistakably "derailed" and become a troublemaker in every harmony of creation. This is becoming more and more apparent from day to day.

But here too, in their favorite game of shifting responsibility, most people quickly come to the conclusion that they themselves have no part in the chaos, but that it is only others who have caused all the misery. They also like to conclude that our species is simply a "misconstruction." The failure therefore happened to God, who created humans with errors. But that is not true! God created us and endowed us with free will ! This free will is an unparalleled privilege, because it allows us to take the path of our choosing and immerse ourselves in the diversity of life according to our wishes. We are therefore allowed to determine the direction and type of our development ourselves and normally lead a life that fully corresponds to our inclinations and abilities. If this does not work, which is often the case, it is only because self-created constraints prevent us from doing so for long periods of time.

Of course, free will also comes with full responsibility for using this gift from the Creator wisely and responsibly. Another help in creation is the law of interaction , which brings us the same consequences when we make mistakes and thus makes us aware of our wrong actions. With good intentions, we have the opportunity to do better in the future and at the same time correct the mistake. But the gift of free will in no way includes a license to spread suffering and destroy our livelihoods. Anyone who expects something like that has not yet given sufficient thought to the unacceptable consequences of such an attitude!

The mere fact that we are still here on earth proves that we have not yet developed into people who faithfully fulfill God's will and his laws of creation - because then we would have been able to ascend to higher regions long ago and would no longer be here.

There is hardly anything more important for all of us than to delve into the nature of our "free will"! We should spare no effort; for it is the most important thing for us, with which we initiate everything for our good or harm! If we know it thoroughly and act accordingly , then the path to ascension is before us! Therefore, I strongly recommend working through the relevant article on free will intensively, as it contains the basic information. -

